---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Employee Health Insurance in Cambodia | AG Cambodia"
  description="Employee health insurance in Cambodia for small teams, SMEs and larger companies: local or international cover, benefit levels by role, and a local broker to manage the programme."
  quoteHref="#form"
>
  <!-- Page hero -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-hero-grid">
        <div class="page-hero-copy">
          <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
            <a href="/">Home</a>
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <a href="/health-insurance-cambodia/">Health Insurance</a>
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <span>Employee &amp; Staff Insurance</span>
          </nav>
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Health Insurance – Corporate Insurance</p>
          <h1>Employee Health Insurance in Cambodia</h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">Providing health insurance is one of the most practical benefits a company can offer its employees. For staff, it means easier access to private healthcare when they need it. For employers, it provides a structured way to support employee wellbeing while strengthening the overall benefits package offered by the company.</p>
          <div class="hero-ctas">
            <a href="#form" class="btn btn-gold">Get a free quote</a>
            <a href="#workforce" class="btn btn-outline-light">How it works</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="page-hero-visual">
          <img src="/assets/employee-benefit.webp" alt="Two colleagues chatting in an office corridor" width="600" height="400" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Designed around your workforce -->
  <section class="section" id="workforce">
    <div class="container article-grid">
      <div class="article-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Built around your team</p>
        <h2>Health insurance designed around your workforce</h2>
        <p>At AG Insurance Broker, we design Employee Health Insurance plans in Cambodia for businesses of different sizes, from small teams and growing SMEs to larger companies with Cambodian and expatriate employees.</p>
        <p>Every company is different, and every employee does not necessarily need the same level of cover. A business may want straightforward local hospitalisation cover for its entire workforce, while providing broader international medical insurance for senior management or expatriate employees.</p>
        <p>Group health insurance can therefore be structured with different levels of benefits according to employee category, seniority or role. Spouses and dependent children may also be added to eligible plans.</p>
        <p>This flexibility allows companies to provide meaningful employee benefits while keeping the overall insurance programme within budget.</p>
        <p>We conduct a comprehensive assessment of your organisation, workforce profile, employee protection needs and financial objectives to design tailored and sustainable employee benefits programmes.</p>
        <a href="#form" class="btn btn-gold">Get a free quote</a>
      </div>

      <aside class="peril-card">
        <h3>Depending on the insurer and programme, cover can include</h3>
        <ul class="peril-list">
          <li>Hospitalisation and inpatient treatment</li>
          <li>Outpatient consultations</li>
          <li>Specialist visits</li>
          <li>Diagnostic tests</li>
          <li>Prescribed medication</li>
          <li>Emergency treatment</li>
          <li>Medical evacuation</li>
          <li>Dental care</li>
          <li>Optical benefits</li>
          <li>Maternity options</li>
          <li>Life and disability benefits</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Local or international -->
  <section class="section section-cream">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Where employees are treated</p>
      <h2>Local or international medical cover</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">One of the first decisions when setting up an employee health insurance plan in Cambodia is where employees should be able to receive treatment.</p>

      <div class="cov-grid cov-grid-2">
        <article class="cov-card">
          <span class="cov-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M4 21V8l8-5 8 5v13M9 21v-6h6v6M4 21h16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span>
          <span class="cov-tag">Cambodia</span>
          <h3>Local plans</h3>
          <p>Local plans are generally designed around hospitals and clinics within Cambodia and can provide an effective solution for companies seeking essential medical protection for their employees.</p>
          <p>They can be particularly suitable for larger local workforces or businesses looking for a practical healthcare benefit at a controlled cost.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="cov-card">
          <span class="cov-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M3 12h18M12 3c2.5 2.5 3.5 6 3.5 9s-1 6.5-3.5 9c-2.5-2.5-3.5-6-3.5-9s1-6.5 3.5-9Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span>
          <span class="cov-tag">Southeast Asia or worldwide</span>
          <h3>International plans</h3>
          <p>Companies employing expatriates, senior managers or employees who travel regularly may prefer access to a broader medical network. International plans can provide treatment across Southeast Asia or worldwide, depending on the geographical area selected.</p>
          <p>They may also include medical evacuation if appropriate treatment is not available locally.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="notice-box">
        <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></circle><path d="M12 8v5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"></path><circle cx="12" cy="16" r="0.9" fill="currentColor"></circle></svg>
        <p><strong>You don't have to choose just one.</strong> A company can combine different levels of cover within the same overall employee benefits strategy.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- A benefit employees use / small and large companies -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cov-grid cov-grid-2">
        <article class="cov-card">
          <span class="cov-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="9" cy="8" r="3.4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></circle><path d="M3 20c1-3.6 3.6-5.6 6-5.6s5 2 6 5.6M17 8v6M14 11h6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg></span>
          <span class="cov-tag">Employees</span>
          <h3>A benefit employees actually use</h3>
          <p>Employee benefits are most valuable when staff understand them and can actually use them. Health insurance provides employees with something tangible: access to medical treatment when they become sick or injured without having to face the full cost themselves.</p>
          <p>For employers, offering private medical insurance can also strengthen the overall employment package when recruiting and retaining staff.</p>
          <p>In Cambodia's competitive employment market, a well-designed health plan can help demonstrate that the company takes the wellbeing of its employees seriously.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="cov-card">
          <span class="cov-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg></span>
          <span class="cov-tag">Any company size</span>
          <h3>Group Health Insurance for small and large companies</h3>
          <p>Corporate medical insurance is not reserved for multinational companies or businesses with hundreds of employees. AG Cambodia can arrange group health insurance for organisations with different workforce sizes and structures.</p>
          <p>Your programme can evolve as your company grows. Employees can be added or removed as teams change, and benefit levels can be reviewed during renewal as your needs and budget develop.</p>
          <p>The objective is not simply to buy an insurance policy, but to create a health programme that remains practical for both employees and management.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Less administration for HR -->
  <section class="section section-cream">
    <div class="container article-grid">
      <div class="article-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">For your HR team</p>
        <h2>Less administration for your HR team</h2>
        <p>Managing employee health insurance can quickly become another administrative task for HR.</p>
        <p>New employees need to be enrolled. Departing employees need to be removed. Benefits need to be explained, documents collected and claims or hospital questions sometimes followed up with the insurer.</p>
        <p>This is where having a local broker makes a difference. Instead of your HR department having to deal with several different insurer contacts, AG Cambodia provides one local point of contact for the programme.</p>
      </div>

      <aside class="peril-card">
        <h3>We assist with the ongoing administration</h3>
        <ul class="peril-list">
          <li>Employee enrolment</li>
          <li>Policy amendments</li>
          <li>Adding and removing employees</li>
          <li>Renewal preparation</li>
          <li>Coordination with insurers</li>
          <li>Questions regarding benefits and eligibility</li>
          <li>Claims assistance</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Cambodian and expatriate employees -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Mixed teams</p>
      <h2>Health insurance for Cambodian and expatriate employees</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Companies with mixed local and international teams often need more than one level of medical insurance.</p>
      <div class="article-copy" style="margin-top: 28px; max-width: 72ch;">
        <p>A Cambodian employee who primarily uses healthcare locally may not require the same geographical coverage as an expatriate executive who wants access to hospitals in Bangkok, Singapore or elsewhere internationally.</p>
        <p>Rather than placing everyone into an unnecessarily expensive single plan, we can help structure different benefit levels while keeping the programme coordinated under one corporate insurance strategy. This allows businesses to balance employee benefits, healthcare access and budget more effectively.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why choose AG -->
  <section class="section section-blue">
    <div class="container article-grid">
      <div class="article-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Why choose us</p>
        <h2>Why choose AG Insurance Broker?</h2>
        <p>Choosing an Employee Health Insurance plan is not simply about comparing premiums.</p>
        <p>Hospital networks, annual limits, outpatient benefits, geographical coverage, deductibles, exclusions, maternity conditions and medical evacuation can make two apparently similar plans very different.</p>
        <p>AG Insurance Broker has been operating in Cambodia since 2006. As an insurance broker, we compare available solutions and help companies understand the differences before selecting a plan.</p>
        <p>Your company therefore has both access to the insurance market and a local team available to help manage the programme after it has been put in place.</p>
        <div class="hero-ctas">
          <a href="https://t.me/Marc_AGCambodia" class="btn btn-telegram" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 4 3 11l6 2m12-9-4 16-8-6m0 0 3-2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg> Contact Marc on Telegram</a>
          <a href="https://t.me/Marie_AGCambodia" class="btn btn-telegram" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 4 3 11l6 2m12-9-4 16-8-6m0 0 3-2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg> Contact Marie on Telegram</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="peril-card">
        <h3>We can help you</h3>
        <ul class="peril-list">
          <li>Assess the needs of your workforce</li>
          <li>Compare local and international insurance solutions</li>
          <li>Create different benefit levels where appropriate</li>
          <li>Understand hospital networks and coverage limits</li>
          <li>Manage employee enrolment and changes</li>
          <li>Prepare renewals</li>
          <li>Assist employees and HR teams with insurance questions</li>
          <li>Provide support when claims occur</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Build the right plan -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container article-grid">
      <div class="article-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Getting started</p>
        <h2>Build the right health plan for your employees</h2>
        <p>Whether you employ five people or manage a much larger workforce, the right solution starts with understanding your team.</p>
        <p>We can then compare suitable Employee Health Insurance options in Cambodia and help you build a programme that works for both your employees and your company.</p>
        <p>Ask AG Insurance Broker for a quotation and let us compare the available plans for your team.</p>
        <a href="#form" class="btn btn-gold">Get a free quote</a>
      </div>

      <aside class="peril-card">
        <h3>Tell us</h3>
        <ul class="peril-list">
          <li>How many employees you want to insure</li>
          <li>Their approximate age range</li>
          <li>Whether employees are Cambodian, expatriate or a combination of both</li>
          <li>The level of healthcare you want to provide</li>
          <li>Whether you need local, regional or worldwide cover</li>
          <li>Your approximate budget</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
      <div class="notice-box">
        <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></circle><path d="M12 8v5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"></path><circle cx="12" cy="16" r="0.9" fill="currentColor"></circle></svg>
        <p>Benefits, hospital networks, eligibility, exclusions, geographical limits and policy conditions vary according to the insurer and plan selected.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Contact / Quote -->
  <section class="section quote-section" id="form">
    <div class="container quote-grid">
      <div class="quote-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Get a quote</p>
        <h2>Your free employee health insurance quote</h2>
        <p class="section-lead section-lead-light">Tell us about your team. Compare offers from multiple insurers with clear, professional advice.</p>
        <ul class="check-list check-list-light">
          <li>We compare 15+ insurers to get you the best rate</li>
          <li>Available in French and English</li>
          <li>Officially licensed and registered in Cambodia</li>
          <li>Fully confidential — your request is never spammed</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="quote-cta-row">
          <a href="https://t.me/AGCambodia" class="btn btn-outline-light" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M21 4 3 11l6 2m12-9-4 16-8-6m0 0 3-2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>
            Telegram
          </a>
          <a href="tel:+85523998018" class="btn btn-outline-light">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M6.6 10.8c1.4 2.8 3.8 5.2 6.6 6.6l2.2-2.2c.3-.3.7-.4 1-.2 1.1.4 2.3.6 3.6.6.6 0 1 .4 1 1V20c0 .6-.4 1-1 1C10.9 21 3 13.1 3 3.5c0-.6.4-1 1-1H7.7c.6 0 1 .4 1 1 0 1.3.2 2.5.6 3.6.1.4 0 .8-.2 1L6.6 10.8Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>
            Call us
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="quote-form-card">
        <p class="quote-form-title">Company &amp; get covered</p>
        <p class="quote-form-sub">Tell us a bit about your team and a broker will call you back within 24 hours.</p>

        <div class="quote-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Insurance type">
          <button type="button" class="quote-tab is-active" role="tab" aria-selected="true">Health Insurance</button>
          <button type="button" class="quote-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Vehicle</button>
          <button type="button" class="quote-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Property</button>
          <button type="button" class="quote-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Other</button>
        </div>

        <form id="quote-form" novalidate>
          <div class="form-row">
            <div class="form-field">
              <label for="firstName">First name *</label>
              <input id="firstName" name="firstName" type="text" required autocomplete="given-name" />
            </div>
            <div class="form-field">
              <label for="lastName">Last name *</label>
              <input id="lastName" name="lastName" type="text" required autocomplete="family-name" />
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="form-row">
            <div class="form-field">
              <label for="email">Email *</label>
              <input id="email" name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="email" />
            </div>
            <div class="form-field">
              <label for="phone">Phone / WhatsApp *</label>
              <input id="phone" name="phone" type="tel" required autocomplete="tel" />
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="form-field">
            <label for="message">Message</label>
            <textarea id="message" name="message" rows="4"></textarea>
          </div>
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-gold btn-block">Request my free quote <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
          <p class="form-note">
            <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><rect x="5" y="11" width="14" height="9" rx="1.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"></rect><path d="M8 11V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"></path></svg>
            Your information is 100% confidential
          </p>
          <p class="form-status" id="form-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
